{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-104023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/assets/8ee061e9348ada782791fca64a55923834dc87393518e9ec41c49698bfb2f92e.png)\n\nWhat are the points of discontinuity of the function plotted above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"} {"question" "q-104023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The graph breaks at $x=-2$ and $x=0,$ meaning that we can't draw the plot without taking our pencil off of the paper when passing through these points.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x=-2$ and $x=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"} {"question" "q-104023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b70db5e58cf13a0c83f5edb33b2e6e4d50dc842bc70a50f0d35bf7cdf37be32a"} {"question" "q-104023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"} {"question" "q-104023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=\\pm 2"] ["text" "$x=-2$ and $x=0$"] ["text" "$x=-2$ only"] ["text" "$x=0$ and $x=2$"] ["text" "$x=0$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"} {"question" "q-104023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$x=-2$ and $x=0$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"} {"question" "q-104025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/assets/2d342689f9e4a213ac5407ccc132868b51ba218afabda1a871e7ca7b02345a17.png)\n\nWhat are the points of discontinuity of the function plotted above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"} {"question" "q-104025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The graph breaks at $x=-1$ and $x=2,$ meaning that we can't draw the plot without taking our pencil off of the paper when passing through these points.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x=-1$ and $x=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"} {"question" "q-104025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b70db5e58cf13a0c83f5edb33b2e6e4d50dc842bc70a50f0d35bf7cdf37be32a"} {"question" "q-104025" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"} {"question" "q-104025" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$x=-1$ and $x=2$"] ["text" "$x=-1$ only"] ["text" "$x=-2$ and $x=1$"] ["text" "$x=1$ and $x=2$"] ["text" "$x=2$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"} {"question" "q-104025" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$x=-1$ and $x=2$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"} {"question" "q-104049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/assets/5143df65d0f99c6511dc8ab13262831669c88535e19c986dacdb364e04847f58.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is plotted above. \n\n- $f(x)$ is defined at $x=2$\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)\\ne f(2)$\n- $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=2$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"} {"question" "q-104049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is true. We have $f(2)=2.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, from the graph we see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}f(x) & =2, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}f(x) & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)=2=f(2).$\n\n- Statement III is false. The graph of the function doesn't have a break at $x=2$ and we can draw the graph of $f(x)$ around $x=2$ without taking our pencil off of the paper." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"} {"question" "q-104049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b70db5e58cf13a0c83f5edb33b2e6e4d50dc842bc70a50f0d35bf7cdf37be32a"} {"question" "q-104049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"} {"question" "q-104049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"} {"question" "q-104049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"} {"question" "q-104051" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/assets/65b9b32e8fac6a71141ce820855058367e9235129de7334db35a200905474cc0.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true? \n\n- $f(x)$ is defined at $x=5$\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\,5}f(x)$ exists\n- $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=5$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"} {"question" "q-104051" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $f(5)=2.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, from the graph we see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{5}^{-}}f(x) & =2, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{5}^{+}}f(x) & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,  ${lim}_{x\\to \\,5}f(x)$ doesn't exist\n\n- Statement III is true. The graph of the function has a jump exactly at $x=5$\nand it's impossible to draw the graph without taking our pencil off of the paper." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"} {"question" "q-104051" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b70db5e58cf13a0c83f5edb33b2e6e4d50dc842bc70a50f0d35bf7cdf37be32a"} {"question" "q-104051" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"} {"question" "q-104051" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"} {"question" "q-104051" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"} {"question" "q-104052" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/assets/8086893e4587e68f8257b75f2070cf622fa141199d6bd8960f7c4fd8e7bcb349.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true? \n\n- $f(x)$ is **not** defined at $x=0$\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}f(x)$ exists\n- $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"} {"question" "q-104052" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is true. From the graph we can see that no value has been assigned to $f(x)$ at $x=0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}f(x) & =3, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{+}}f(x) & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}f(x)=3.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function is not even defined at $x=0.$ The graph contains a break at $x=0.$ It's impossible to draw the graph of $f(x)$ without taking our pencil off of the paper." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"} {"question" "q-104052" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b70db5e58cf13a0c83f5edb33b2e6e4d50dc842bc70a50f0d35bf7cdf37be32a"} {"question" "q-104052" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"} {"question" "q-104052" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"} {"question" "q-104052" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980965/state.json" "file_sha256" "b9c92d0784d6db1815ebe398b0b03e71eb5977dc7a956ee75bc7b81c2e9f4477"}] "usage" {} "basis" 877 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
